#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:5
msgid "My account"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:7
msgid "This page is written for the members of your association. It explains what a member can see and do once logged in to Galette. You can send them a link to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:11
msgid "Some of what is described here depends on choices made by the association: a feature that is not displayed for you has probably been disabled in the :ref:`preferences <man_preferences>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:14
msgid "Logging in"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:16
msgid "Your association gives you a username and a password, often by email when your member card is created. On the login page, type either your **username** or your **email address**, then your password, and click on **Login**."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:18
msgid "Galette login page"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:23
msgid "If your association allows it, a **Register** button at the top of the page lets people who are not members yet fill in a membership request themselves."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:25
msgid "The language of the interface can be changed at any time from the list at the top right of the page."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:28
msgid "Forgotten or new password"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:30
msgid "If you do not remember your password - or if it's not been set yet, click on **Lost your password?** under the login form. This link is only displayed when your association has configured the sending of emails."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:32
msgid "Password recovery page"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:37
msgid "Type your username or your email address, and click on **Recover password**. If an account matches, Galette will send an email to you."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:39
msgid "The email you receive contains a link. Follow it, then type your new password twice and click on **Change my password**. The link only works once, and for 24 hours."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:43
msgid "No email received? Check your spam folder first. If your member card holds no email address, or an invalid one, no message can be sent: ask a staff member to fix your account information."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:46
msgid "Your dashboard"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:48
msgid "After logging in, you reach your dashboard. It gives a quick access to your information, your contributions and your transactions."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:50
msgid "Dashboard of a member"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:55
msgid "The same pages are listed in the **My Account** menu, on the left:"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:57
msgid "**My contributions**,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:58
msgid "**My scheduled payments**,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:59
msgid "**My transactions**,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:60
msgid "**My information**."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:62
msgid "**Two-factor authentication** and **Add a child member** may also be listed there, when your association has enabled them."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:65
msgid "My information"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:67
msgid "**My information** displays your member card: your identity, your contact information, the groups you belong to, the state of your membership, ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:69
msgid "Member card, as seen by the member"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:74
msgid "The state of your membership is displayed under your picture:"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:76
msgid "**X days remaining (ending on ...)**: your membership is up to date,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:77
msgid "**Last day!**: your membership ends today,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:78
msgid "**Late of X days (since ...)**: your membership has expired, it is time to renew it,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:79
msgid "**Never contributed**: no membership fee has been recorded for you yet,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:80
msgid "**Freed of dues**: you do not have to pay membership fees."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:83
msgid "Changing your information"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:85
msgid "Click on **Modification** to change your information, then on **Save** at the bottom of the form. Your association decides which fields you can change: the others are read only, or not displayed at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:87
msgid "To change your password, type the new one in **Password:** and again in **Password confirmation:**. Leave both fields empty to keep your current password."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:90
msgid "Other actions"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:92
msgid "The small arrow next to the **Modification** button opens more actions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:94
msgid "Actions available on the member card"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:99
msgid "**Generate Member Card**: download your member card as a PDF file. It is only available when your membership is up to date, and when your association allows members to print their card,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:100
msgid "**Adhesion form**: download your adhesion form as a PDF file, filled in with your information,"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:101
msgid "**View contributions**: the list of your contributions."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:103
msgid "The small card icon next to your name downloads your contact information as a vCard file, that most address books can import."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:106
msgid "My contributions"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:108
msgid "**My contributions** lists the membership fees and donations recorded for you. Each line shows the dates, the type, the amount and the payment type of the contribution."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:110
msgid "List of the contributions of a member"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:115
msgid "The PDF icon of the **Actions** column downloads an invoice or a receipt for the contribution, depending on its type."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:117
msgid "The filters at the top of the list help to find a contribution: by date, by payment type or by contribution type. Click on **Filter** to apply them, and on **Clear filter** to come back to the whole list."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:119
msgid "You cannot add or change a contribution yourself."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:122
msgid "My transactions and scheduled payments"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:124
msgid "A transaction is a payment that covers several contributions; for example, a single check that pays both a membership fee and a donation. **My transactions** lists the transactions recorded for you."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:126
msgid "**My scheduled payments** lists the payments that are planned for your contributions, when your association lets you pay in several times."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:128
msgid "Both lists are read only, as for contributions."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:131
msgid "Adding a child member"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:133
msgid "If your association allows it, **Add a child member** in the **My Account** menu lets you create the member card of a child, or of any person you are responsible for. That card is then attached to yours: you can see and change it, and see its contributions. See also :ref:`links between members <linkmembers>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:136
msgid "Two-factor authentication"
msgstr ""

#: ../usermanual/my_account.rst:138
msgid "When your association has enabled it, you can protect your account with a code that changes every thirty seconds, in addition to your password. This is described in :ref:`two-factor authentication <man_2fa>`."
msgstr ""
